					<![CDATA[
						 <div style="text-align: right;"></div> <p><strong>Date:</strong> 15-7-20██</p> <p><strong>Approved by:</strong> Dr. To██ ███.</p> <hr /> <p><strong>Subject/s:</strong> two subjects have been selected to enter scp-5212, D-24576-A male, 36yrs and D-8697-B male, 24yrs. Both have been equipped with a headset with a built in camera, a satchel bag, a hand held torch, and a small bottle of water.</p> <p>Both subjects are instructed to enter scp-5212, with the front door being left open, the two are then instructed to take the same course as the previous expedition but to make a slight deviation into one of the rooms. The two then enter one of the rooms in the longer hallway, with the camera picking up another hallway inside of the room.</p> <p>Both subjects are to make an effort in finding more textbooks amongst the clutter. Subject A then finds one, with subject A being ordered to return to control with his find. Subject B is to continue deeper into scp-5212-1. Subject 2 protests at first, but control convinces him to proceed.</p> <p>Subject B carries on through the hallway, control then orders them to take a sample of the wall material. Subject B comments on the density of the wall, and that a piece cannot be removed. Control then instructs them to find a piece that's already broken off, but this request is not carried through as there is no indication of damage to any of the walls.</p> <p>Subject B is then ordered to proceed to the end of the hallway, with the camera looking out for any indication of hand written notes. Once subject B gets to the end, he finds a T junction. The right hallway is viewed to have another T junction at its end, while the left has a closed door. Control then orders them to proceed to the closed door.</p> <p>Subject B is then instructed to open the door, they comply and open it, but are stopped when the door doesn't open out fully. They try to open it with more force, but it still doesn't open. Control instructs him to see what is keeping it closed, Subject B begins to panic, with the camera showing an unidentifiable hand holding the other doorknob. The door slams shut, control orders them to try and open it again, Subject B is still panicking, and asks to leave, control accepts his request but instructs him to search for more writing of any sort.</p> <p>Subject B is not successful in acquiring anything. Control then instructs them to return to the start of the T junction, they then reach the junction, but the hallway now leads to the entrance, where control orders him to exit scp-5212. The front door is shut behind him.</p> <hr /> <p><strong>Post expedition report:</strong> Subject D-24576-A retrieved another textbook, illustrations now included, showing a ball, a shoe, and coin. Subject D-8697-B did not retrieve anything, however the discovery of scp-5212-2 has now completely changed our approach towards scp-5212. We now also believe these notes we have picked up have been written by scp-5212-2 More evidence now suggests that scp-5212-1 is intentionally leading subjects out of the house, motive still unknown.</p> <p><strong>Signed:</strong> Dr. To██ ███.</p> <hr /> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sami-gibbons" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6346785&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607372471" alt="Sami Gibbons" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6346785)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/sami-gibbons" >Sami Gibbons</a></span></p> 
